{"verdict":"approved","issues":[{"severity":"minor","file":"src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts","line":126,"description":"Missing trailing newline at end of file (\\ No newline at end of file in diff).","suggestedFix":"Add a trailing newline at the end of the file."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.spec.ts","line":97,"description":"The getDiscount helper function lacks an explicit return type annotation, which violates the TypeScript strict compliance criterion that all function return types be explicitly typed.","suggestedFix":"Add an explicit return type: function getDiscount(dispatch: MozioDispatchPayload): PriceDiscount { ... }"}],"summary":"The implementation correctly addresses the prescribed root cause: the filter in applyReportDiscountsService was comparing Mozio dispatch lineItem.id (a composite key like `<orderLineItemId>#return`) directly against discount.lineItemId (the original BigCommerce order line item ID), causing zero matches for return trips. The fix reuses the existing parseDispatchLineItemKey helper (from src/services/helpers/order/dispatch-line-item-key.ts) to extract the original order line item ID from the composite key before comparison — exactly the prescribed minimal fix. No hand-rolled logic; no over-engineering. The diff is 9 insertions / 4 deletions in the service file plus a new 151-line spec file.\n\nTest coverage: 3 vitest tests covering (1) return trip discount applied, (2) outbound non-return discount still works (no regression), (3) round trip with both outbound and return discounts. All tests pass (exit 0). tsc --noEmit also exits 0.\n\nAcceptance criteria verification:\n- Return trip shows promo code discount amount: ✓ (test 1 verifies amount.value=10, selling=90)\n- Correct discount value for return trip: ✓ (test 1 and test 3 verify correct amounts)\n- No regression for outbound trips: ✓ (test 2 verifies outbound still works; test 3 verifies both in a round trip)\n- Promo code discount name displayed for return trips: ✓ (all tests assert name is Code:SAVE10)\n\nOnly minor issues: missing trailing newline and one missing return type annotation in the test helper."}
